Theorem RL-comp: whole-suite composition — RL-1..RL-34 realization equals plain ARC

  Preconditions:
    - This is the sec-08.12 composition theorem per the sec-08
      success_criteria: RL-1..RL-34 applied to a realized ArcFunction produce
      observably equivalent behavior to plain ARC on the same function.
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - Each constituent RL-N is proved by its own theorem (RL-1.proof ..
      RL-34.proof + RL-11a / RL-14a / RL-15a / RL-18a + the RL-13 removal
      confirmation); RL-comp composes them into the joined claim.
    - depends-on every RL-N (the constituent realization rules) + the
      RL-1/RL-2 multi-use Let Var composition.

  Soundness property:
    Forall realized ArcFunction F:

      (P1) Joined equivalence: applying the full realization rule set
           (RL-1..RL-34, with the RL-13 removal and the RL-11a/14a/15a/18a
           sub-rules) to F produces an ArcFunction whose observable behavior
           equals plain ARC on F. Each constituent rule is a refinement of
           plain ARC (RC-count preserving, value-semantics preserving, or
           layout/escape preserving); their composition preserves the
           conjunction of those properties.

      (P2) Conjunction strength: RL-comp is EXACTLY as strong as the
           conjunction of its constituents — it holds iff every constituent
           RL-N discharges. It never gracious-accepts over a failing or
           missing premise. A dropped constituent leaves a realization rule
           unproven (a false-valid risk), so the coverage gate asserts the
           full active-rule count.

    RL-comp is the capstone of the sec-08 substantive contribution: the proof
    that AIMS realization, rule by rule and composed, is a sound refinement of
    plain ARC — every RC operation in the emitted IR corresponds to a specific
    proof step, and their composition does not introduce a leak, double-free,
    or observable divergence.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the rc_counting engine via composition of all
    discharged RL constituents (mirrors section_07::verify_pl_composition).

    Part (P1/P2) — constituent composition:
      The verifier re-runs each of the 38 RL constituent verifiers (RL-1..5,
      RL-6..10, RL-11/11a/12/13, RL-14/14a/15/15a/16, RL-17/18, RL-18a,
      RL-19..21, RL-22..26, RL-27/28, RL-29/30/31, RL-32/33/34), asserts each
      returns Valid, AND re-runs the RL-1/RL-2 multi-use Let Var composition.
      Coverage gate: exactly 38 RL constituents discharged. A failing or
      missing constituent fails RL-comp (the joined claim is no stronger than
      its weakest premise).

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl_composition; constituent
        re-run + Valid-assertion + 38-count coverage gate; emits Fail on any
        non-discharging constituent or a count mismatch)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 rc_counting engine discharges the whole-suite composition theorem RL-comp by composing all 38 discharged RL constituents (each re-run and asserted Valid) plus the RL-1/RL-2 multi-use Let Var composition, with a 38-count coverage gate ensuring no constituent is dropped — the joined proof that RL-1..RL-34 realization is observably equivalent to plain ARC
